            )
          %h3#the_presheaf_topos_over_nonempty_finite_sets The presheaf topos over non-empty finite sets
          %p
            Just like in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} topos of simpicial sets
            levels in the topos of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+set"} symmetric sets
            correspond to the natural numbers. The computation of the Aufhebungs relation between the levels was an open problem in topos theory since the 1980s. In
            %a{:href => "#HM25"} 2025 Hora and Maehara
            show that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\geq 3
            it is given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n-1
            just like in the topos of simplicial sets.
