          %h2#a_guide_to_the_literature A guide to the literature
          %p
            On the philosophical side, the lectures notes
            %a{:href => "#Koch09"} Koch (2009)
            that suggest the use of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+set"} non-wellfounded set theory
            as interpretative tool may serve as a good general introduction to Hegel’s ideas on logic and metaphysics.
            %a{:href => "#Krahn14"} Krahn (2014)
            considers Hegel’s concept of Aufhebung in the context of postmodern thought. For lucid accounts of Hegel’s concept of dialectics in general consult Brauer (
            %a{:href => "#Brauer82"}> 1982
            ) and Wolff (
            %a{:href => "#Wolff10"}> 2010
            ) the latter highlighting Hegel as ‘a philosopher of mathematics’ in this context. Wegerhoff (
            %a{:href => "#Wegerhoff08"}> 2008
            ) offers an interesting structural account of the dialectics inspired by Dedekind’s theory of natural numbers.
          %p
            On the mathematical side, the book by
            %a{:href => "#RRZ04"} La Palme-Reyes-Zolfaghari (2004)
            provides a good general entry to the ‘mathematics of Lawvere’ from an elementary point of view and contains even a page on the adjoint cylinder. Goldblatt’s book on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Goldblatt84"}> Goldblatt 1984
            ) covers a good deal of ground yet stays accessible and is available online.
          %p
            Lawvere introduced the Hegelian concepts in Lawvere (
            %a{:href => "#Law89b"}> 1989b
            ). They get some attention in Lawvere (
            %a{:href => "#Law91a"}> 1991a
            ,
            %a{:href => "#Law92"}> 1992
            ,
            %a{:href => "#Law94a"}> 1994a
            ) with the second containing his ‘philosophical program’. By all means have a look at
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Law96"} Lawvere (1996)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Law89a"} 1989a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Law99"} 1999
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Law89b"} 1989b
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Law91b"} 1991b
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Law02"} 2002
            %em Aufhebungs
            relation with the latter containing a discussion of the relevant concepts.
            %a{:href => "#KL89"} Kelly-Lawvere (1989)
            provides the technical prerequisites on essential localizations for
            = succeed "." do
              %em Aufhebung
          %p
            The known mathematical results on the Aufhebungs relation are contained in the paper by
            %a{:href => "#KRRZ11"} Kennett-Riehl-Roy-Zaks (2011)
            which is based on older phd-works by some of the authors (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Roy97"} Roy (1997)
          %p
            Further results on essential localizations can be found in the papers by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BK91"} Borceux-Korotenski (1991)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JS96"} Johnstone (1996)
            %a{:href => "#VT01"} Vitale (2001)
            and
            %a{:href => "#LW11"} Lucyshyn-Wright (2011)
            or in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SGA4"} SGA 4
          %hr/
          %p
            %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AufhebungDetail.jpg", :width => "900"}/
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "http://www.in-situ-art-society.com/docs/2015-09-18+19_aufhebung_flyer.pdf"} full pdf
            by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://www.in-situ-art-society.com/aufhebung.html"} In Situ Art Society
